=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A thorough, multi-layer investigation found no network fault. All ICMP probes
from host_1_1_1_1 to every data-centre device (dns_server, web_server_0
through web_server_3) completed with 0 % packet loss and round-trip times in
the expected 1.4–2.0 ms range. An HTTP curl test against web_server_0 also
succeeded normally (~2.7 ms total). The full lab-wide reachability matrix
confirmed that every host-to-host pair is reachable with 0 % loss.

The forwarding path through the building uplink was explicitly verified:
switch_dist_1_1 is UP with its br0 gateway (10.1.1.1) correctly configured,
its eth0 link to router_core_1 is UP, and its single OSPF neighborship with
router_core_1 is in Full state. router_core_1 in turn holds Full OSPF
adjacencies with router_core_2, router_core_3, and switch_dist_1_1, and
carries a valid FIB entry for 10.200.0.0/24 via router_core_3. router_core_3
and switch_server_access are equally healthy, with all adjacencies Full and
all prefixes correctly installed. No interface shows any errors or dropped
packets.

The ticket's claim that "the entire data centre went away" is not supported by
any evidence in the live lab. The network is operating exactly as designed.
The most likely explanation is a transient glitch (brief interface flap or
OSPF reconvergence) that had already self-healed before this investigation
began, or the user may have been experiencing a client-side issue unrelated to
the network infrastructure. No corrective action is required on the network.
